<div style="text-align: center">

# <span style="color: #e6a050">Grimoire - Spells and Arrows Slots</span>

</div>

<div style="text-align: center">

*<span style="color: #e6a050">Your spells and arrows in slots of their own, out of the backpack, in the order you choose.</span>*

</div>

<div style="text-align: center">

The source code for all my Enshrouded mods is available on [GitHub](https://github.com/Fuzen777/Enshrouded-Mods) (MIT)

</div>

---

Grimoire is a **Kiln** mod that keeps your spells and arrows in a grimoire of their own instead of your backpack. Each kind of spell or arrow gets one slot, the HUD's spell and arrow lists follow the order you set, and picking one in the HUD equips it as usual.

It works with the game's own equipment, not around it, so it doesn't always behave the way you might expect. **Please read the Caveats below before you install it.**

---

## Caveats

### The Equipped One Still Takes a Backpack Slot

- The game only casts a spell (or fires an arrow) from your backpack or hotbar, so **the equipped spell and the equipped arrows each keep one slot there**. Everything else stays in the grimoire.
- Switching swaps the new pick into that same slot and puts the old one back in the grimoire, so you never need more than that one slot.
- With nothing equipped and a **full backpack**, a spell can't be equipped from the grimoire. Free one slot.
- If the equipped spell sits on your hotbar, it stays there, and the spells you switch to take its place. When switching extremely fast, it can move to another hotbar slot, but it is always just that one spell.

### Only in a World You Host

- Grimoire works in **single player** and for the **host** of a co-op world. A player who joins someone else's world gets the game's own lists, and their grimoire does nothing there.
- Not tested on dedicated servers.

### What Joins the Grimoire by Itself

- Any spell or arrow **already in your grimoire** that shows up in your backpack (looted, crafted, picked up, or the one you just switched away from) is filed into the grimoire within about a second, unless it is the equipped one.
- Spells and arrows you never added stay in your backpack, and you can still pick them from the HUD. Picking one puts the grimoire's equipped one back in the grimoire.
- **Take Out** (right-click in the grimoire window) removes a spell from the grimoire for good, so it stops being filed in again.

### Removing the Mod

- Kiln keeps the grimoire's contents with your character, **outside the backpack**. Without Grimoire installed, they stay stored but out of reach until you install it again.
- **Before you uninstall**, open the grimoire (F3) and press **Take All Out** on both the Spells and the Arrows tab, with enough free backpack slots. Then save.
- Turning **Mod Enabled** off brings back the game's own lists, but the grimoire keeps what it holds. Take everything out first if you want it back in your backpack.

### HUD Lists

- The HUD shows the grimoire's spells first, in your order, then the other spells in your backpack.
- When the list has hidden itself, moving to one of the grimoire's spells doesn't bring it back the way moving to a backpack spell does. The pick still works. That's a Kiln limit (reported).
- While you switch spells very quickly, the game sometimes empties the spell slot for a moment. Grimoire puts the spell back, so you may see the HUD flash no spell for a split second.

### Death

- The grimoire is kept on death. The equipped spell and arrows are in your backpack, so the game's own rules apply to them.

### Other Mods

- Don't use it together with another mod that changes the HUD's spell or arrow list, like **Quiver & Spellbook**. If you're replacing Quiver & Spellbook, move its hidden spells and arrows back into your backpack and save **before** you remove it, or they will be lost.

---

## Features

### Grimoire Window

- Opens with **F3** (or the **Open Grimoire** button on the mod's page in Kiln's menu), with a **Spells** tab and an **Arrows** tab. It opens on Spells, unless you only have arrows to sort.
- Click an entry to equip it, drag to reorder, right-click (or drag it onto the backpack list) to take it out.
- The spells or arrows in your backpack are listed below: click one or drag it in to add it. **Ctrl+Click** a spell or arrow in the game's inventory adds it too. **Add All** and **Take All Out** move everything at once.

### Settings

- **Mod Enabled**: off gives you the game's own lists back. The grimoire keeps what it holds.
- **Spell Slots** and **Arrow Slots** (1 to 32, default 12): how many kinds the grimoire holds, one slot each. More of a kind already in it tops up its slot. Lowering it keeps what is already in it.

### Running Out

- When a charged spell or a stack of arrows runs out, more of the same is equipped from the grimoire, otherwise the next one in your order.

---

## Requirements

- [Kiln](https://github.com/frostdev-ops/kiln) mod loader, **0.2.0-dev.31 or newer** (Kiln's player storage).

## Installation

1. Close the game.
2. Drop the archive on Kiln.
3. Start the game and load a world you host.
4. Press F3, then add your spells and arrows.

**Changing the key**: it is **Open Grimoire** in the Keys tab of Kiln's menu. The settings are kept in Kiln's profile, so updating the mod never resets them.

---

## Credits

- The Kiln team, for the loader, its player storage and the HUD list API this mod is built on.
